    "summary": "The confirm_wait token-forgery fix adds t5's own 'security-review' kind to the daemon's SHARED step-state store (src/daemon/threads/step-state.ts) -- the same registry insrc_workflow_step's own state-store.ts already uses for identical opaque-continuation-token purposes; this is the idiomatic, established mechanism for this exact need, not a one-off. The durable degraded-disposition fix threads a `degraded` field through t4's own SecurityReviewReport/runSecurityReview contract (run-security-review.ts), the only place that owns the report object this Task needs to carry the flag on; t4 was independently re-validated passing (all 10 of its own acceptance checks hold) after this change. This turn also removed a duplicate local containment check in favor of actually calling run-security-review.ts's own exported assertTargetsContained. No sibling Task's own behavior changed; t2/t3/t4 were each independently re-validated passing after these commits.",
